{
    "intro": [
      {
        "title": "will · would · must · should — and how to say no",
        "title_cz": "will · would · must · should — a jak říct ne",
        "body": "These short words go **in front of** the verb and change what the sentence does:\n**will** — you promise to do it.\n**would like** — a polite way to ask.\n**must** — you have to do it.\n**should** — it is a good idea.\nTo say *no*, or to ask a question in the present, English needs **do** or **does**: *Do you live here?* · *He does not drink coffee.*",
        "note_cz": "Čeština pomocné do/does nemá — v angličtině je ale povinné."
      },
      {
        "title": "You will use these frames",
        "frames": [
          "I will …",
          "I would like …",
          "I must …",
          "You should …",
          "I cannot …",
          "Do you …?",
          "Does he …?",
          "I do not …"
        ],
        "note": "After **will**, **must**, **should** and **can**, the verb stays in its basic form — no *to*, and no *-s* for he / she / it.",
        "note_cz": "Po will / must / should / can je sloveso v základním tvaru."
      }
    ],
